                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "be37c6ab-f6d8-3b8e-bf07-88cb7ba5f8f1",
                        "entry_id": "a6ae32e4-6f6c-3581-aa25-1ded49d3d1ac",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To bleed more than; to lose more blood than."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "39355afb-1391-4c83-8138-a8db5e167be3",
                                "sense_id": "be37c6ab-f6d8-3b8e-bf07-88cb7ba5f8f1",
                                "text": "And there is enough gore to outbleed “Ben-Hur.”"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5d10cee5-5a17-4ef3-9496-1150871f4406",
                                "sense_id": "be37c6ab-f6d8-3b8e-bf07-88cb7ba5f8f1",
                                "text": "But my heart is bigger than your heart, And I will outbleed you."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9ce5a7b8-9e75-400b-96fe-42d4219ac94e",
                                "sense_id": "be37c6ab-f6d8-3b8e-bf07-88cb7ba5f8f1",
                                "text": "Though one autumn morning poppies may suddenly flare out in full bloom, their skirts outrageously seeming to outbleed a maimed human being"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "990b1954-54e5-43b8-bb4b-baade5e2305e",
                                "sense_id": "be37c6ab-f6d8-3b8e-bf07-88cb7ba5f8f1",
                                "text": "Now he realizes that he has more blood than she does, and can probably outbleed her, but he's about to faint even, before cutting himself, and he decides to forfeit, and she wins. Never get into a bleeding contest with a suicidal girl!"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "466f7303-d6af-3722-a3e1-b2b1d21d2323",
                        "entry_id": "a6ae32e4-6f6c-3581-aa25-1ded49d3d1ac",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To win (a battle) by being willing to accept more casualties or injuries."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "figuratively",
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "dc5b1f1c-a1ac-41c4-aa59-9550a8cd6d27",
                                "sense_id": "466f7303-d6af-3722-a3e1-b2b1d21d2323",
                                "text": "The conflict in Europe must inevitably show that the standard of justice is not established by the power of one nation to outbleed another."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ce95583f-a460-4f3d-a55b-7422b23641de",
                                "sense_id": "466f7303-d6af-3722-a3e1-b2b1d21d2323",
                                "text": "Warren had tried to act rationally and humanely under a general whose main strategy was to bludgeon his opponent to death, to outbleed him."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
